   },
   "rtf": 0.2957965812970371,
   "id": "en_long_04",
   "lang": "en",
   "length": "long",
   "units": 84,
   "text": "Astronomers announced the discovery of a small rocky planet orbiting a dim red star about forty light years from Earth. The planet completes one orbit every eleven days and receives roughly the same amount of starlight that Earth receives from the sun, placing it inside the region where liquid water could exist. The team plans to use a large space telescope to search for signs of an atmosphere, though they caution that it will take years to gather enough data to draw firm conclusions."
  },
  {
   "ttfa_s": 0.05164133300422691,
   "total_s": 10.587211457983358,
   "audio_s": 36.24,
   "sample_rate": 24000,
   "num_bytes": 1739520,
