   },
   "rtf": 0.2991154177569616,
   "id": "en_long_06",
   "lang": "en",
   "length": "long",
   "units": 79,
   "text": "The old bookshop on the corner survived for decades by refusing to specialize. Its shelves held cookbooks next to poetry, repair manuals next to novels, and maps of countries that no longer existed. The owner knew most of her customers by name and could often guess what they wanted before they asked. When the building was finally sold, the neighborhood organized a farewell party, and people lined up around the block to buy one last book and say goodbye."
  },
